A||||28||Oreif||N.I.F.E.'s Fierorama 2000! Who is going?||||1||
Z||000000||Oreif||08-28-2000||12:31 AM||||Sunday September 10 Is our clubs annual car show. It is for the "daily driver" cars. Many door prizes and raffles! If you want to show off your Fiero this is the place to do it! Cars are broken down into years, styles, (fastback/notchback) and mileage. So even if you have high miles you still have a good chance of winning. There are awards for most distance traveled to get to the show and "hard luck" cars (they have to be driven not towed) (Haze, orange ones in bad taste don't count     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> ) Come on out and have some FUN! Here is a hint of the great prizes.<BR>Hint: Wanna put a V-8 in a Fiero? Someone is going to raffle one of his kits.<BR>For pre-registration contact Paul Vargyas at paulv@xnet.com<P>NIFE = Northern Illinois Fiero Enthusiasts.<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">    <P><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 08-28-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||SilverFieroV6||08-28-2000||12:57 AM||||sorry i am new to the board.  where is this being held at????, i prob wont enter as heads are sitting off the car right now but would still like to show up and maybe meet a few people and take in the scenery of nice cas||||reg||5
Z||000002||Oreif||08-28-2000||01:00 AM||||I'm sorry I forgot to say where!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"><BR>It's at:<BR>2111 Midwest Road<BR>Oak Brook, ILL<BR>You can use any mapping program or get driving directions from Yahoo.<P>BTW ~ Welcome to our little part of the internet.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 08-28-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||SilverFieroV6||08-28-2000||01:31 AM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">  i think  ILL is a little to far for me, the fall fiero show seems a little more in my area to get to.    <BR>thanks for the info<BR>Sam||||reg||8
Z||000004||Haze_Performance||08-28-2000||08:21 AM||||The only way Ill show up is if they raffle off a 5 Ton floor jack  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> lol (Inside Joke).<P>Ill be there. I wouldnt miss it .....<P>Come on guy's this will be the largest Fiero Event of the year. Where else can you see well over 100 Fiero's in one place?? DONT MISS IT  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mycarsig.jpg">  <B>My 1985 2M4 Sport Coupe </B><P><BR><B>My Website's  <A HREF="http://www.drive.to/WS6_Fiero.com" TARGET=_blank>WS6 Fiero</A> &                  <A HREF="http://www.drive.to/HMP" TARGET=_blank>H.M.P. </A></B>||||reg||4
Z||000005||whamel||08-28-2000||08:42 AM||||Me! Me!  I'm very much planning on going!  Since I couldn't get any time to work on my car this past weekend, I even put it in the shop so they can fix my electrical problem before the show!  I will be bringing my '86 notchback GT.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Of course, I'll probably get the hard luck award since I just ripped my #%$#! entire front clip off the car putting it on the trailer Sunday.  ARGH!  So nobody laugh, okay?    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>Unfortunately, if the shop can't get my electrical problem sorted out, I'll be driving the 2F4 Ranger instead - but regardless, I'm going to be there!<p>[This message has been edited by whamel (edited 08-28-2000).]||||reg||1
